{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790605205,"nonce":"SRi93jv/3OLIYHT0IeIeLerISzc=","title":"Recover Agent when new session creation fails","message":"## Problem\n\nIn the desktop tutor, entering /new while an answer streams aborts the active request before awaiting native createAgentSession. If native session creation rejects, use-agent.ts leaves status as streaming, clears the command from the composer, and allows an unhandled rejection. The Stop control remains visible although the active controller has been cleared.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Reproduce a real native session-creation failure with the desktop bridge and assert a visible actionable error, no unhandled rejection, and a usable composer instead of a stuck streaming state.\n- Preserve prior conversation state if a replacement session could not be created; do not claim a new session exists.\n- Successful /new during streaming still cancels the answer, clears messages, and leaves a ready Agent.\n\nThis is separate from the compact model-picker presentation; do not add a test-only DOM flag or stub native failure in browser E2E.","files":null}]}